# Rust Architecture Guide (LLM Rulebook)

## Purpose

Basic architecture principles for Rust applications. Apply when designing application structure. DO NOT apply to existing codebases.

## Design Principles (MUST)

- Follow SOLID principles
- Prefer composition over inheritance
- Use dependency injection
- Keep functions small and focused

## Application Structure

- Separate business logic from infrastructure
- Use repository pattern for data access
- Group related functionality into modules
- Keep dependencies explicit

```rust
// Good: clear module separation
pub mod domain {
    pub mod entities;
    pub mod services;
}

pub mod infrastructure {
    pub mod repositories;
    pub mod external_apis;
}
```

## Data Access

- Abstract data operations behind traits
- Use repository pattern for consistency
- Keep database details out of business logic

```rust
#[async_trait]
pub trait UserRepository {
    async fn find_by_id(&self, id: i64) -> Result<Option<User>, RepositoryError>;
    async fn save(&self, user: User) -> Result<User, RepositoryError>;
}
```

## Dependency Injection

- Pass dependencies through constructors
- Use traits for testability
- Avoid global state

```rust
pub struct UserService<R> {
    repository: R,
}

impl<R: UserRepository> UserService<R> {
    pub fn new(repository: R) -> Self {
        Self { repository }
    }
}
```

## Out of Scope

- Specific framework implementations
- Database-specific patterns
- Cloud provider specific architectures
- Real-time communication protocols
- Microservices communication patterns